	(lib_symbols)
	(text "BLOCK: power_rails\n\nSCOPE\n  Conversion and distribution of every downstream rail from +24V_SW.\n  Rail set provisional pending the FAFF 2 block diagram SVG; presently\n  evidenced: +5V (load cell 5 V excitation, IKP11 V5 read-head supply),\n  +3V3 (STM32H723, USB3320, DRV8323 logic, QSPI, EEPROM, encoders) and a\n  quiet analog rail / reference pair for the ADS1235 and ADS1120.\n  Producer-owns-the-break rule (DEC-0007): every rail leaves this sheet\n  through its own 0R/jumper isolation link plus a current-measurement break.\n  Budget: ~5.2 W quiescent, 25 W peak (CALC-P-01).\n\nINTERFACES - the binding contract between blocks.\nReconciled against docs/FAFF-2-Electronics-Full.svg (block diagram) and\nhardware/cubemx/ARIA_SRB_FAFF_2_POC_CBs_1.ioc (MCU pin-map authority).\nNeed something not listed here? Raise it - do not invent it.\n  IN   +24V_SW, PGND from power_entry_24v\n  OUT  +5V, +3V3, analog rail(s) + reference, AGND / DGND to all blocks\n  OUT  PGOOD / rail enable lines -> mcu (TBC - no .ioc pin allocated yet)\n  TEST TP + LK + current break per rail (see docs/TEST_PLAN.md)\n\nSTATUS: stub. No circuitry drawn yet - this sheet is reserved for the\nfollow-up block task that owns this file. Invoke /schematic-style before\nthe first edit, and delete this note once the block is drawn."
